findings.description:
"Extend the 320 store, don't fork it" puts snapshots and review findings into `MetrologyStore`. Every `list_*` call in that store globs every `*.json` file, then parses and validates each one with Pydantic, then filters in memory (`store.py:176-189`, `279-304`). The module docstring justifies this as enough "for the join and aggregation this slice needs" (320's).

This component adds:

- one snapshot per commit, per project, with automatic captures at fork and merge;
- one record per review (or per finding) across all historical reviews;
- trend reports that join three record types over time.

Each report call would re-parse the whole user-level store, including every other project's records. The non-goal "No new store" is fine, but the doc should either confirm that full scans stay acceptable at the expected volume or plan a cheap index, such as a per-project/per-type subdirectory or filename prefix. Either works without a schema migration. "No schema migration" should not be read as "no change to how the store is organised on disk".
